 refs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]artifact_link_jumps.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/artifact_link_jumps.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-16t[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-16t/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wildcard matching in the sase-core query evaluator[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-glob[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-glob: in the linked sase-core repo, make `*` a wildcard inside [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]string-field property values (anchored for exact-match fields and `sha`,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unanchored for substring fields, literal for enums), with Rust tests [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proving `id:alpha-1.*` semantics and byte-identical behavior for values [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]without `*`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wildcard parity, pin bump, pushdown guard, and docs in sase[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]host-glob[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-glob[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]host-glob: move the sase-core CI pin past the wildcard commit, mirror [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the semantics in the Python reference evaluator with parity tests, keep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glob values out of Agents-tab index pushdown, and document wildcards in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the query language reference and field hints.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Never lose a pane report, never treat loading as absence[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]seam[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]seam: fix the confirmed root cause (Beads/Plans/Agents/Files resolve a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]request synchronously, the report is dropped during dispatch, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane returns PENDING so the transaction hangs), capture synchronous [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reports at the host seam, make fold-hidden pending targets truthful, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wait on loading panes, re-resolve refs after load, fix project scope [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]handling, re-index hydrated rows, and add real-pane regression tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plan-then-commit reveal engine with Beads context queries[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]planner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-glob, seam[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]planner: replace the trial-and-error limit-drop, widening, and neutral [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rungs with one verified context rewrite (fold, acquire, context, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity, neutral, honest failure), add the `host_reveal_context` pane [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hook, the dialect-aware query renderer, the limit policy, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hidden-reason analysis, and ship the Beads family queries [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](`id:<epic>.*`) end to end.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agent and File context queries plus Agents-tab reveal[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]flat-panes[dim] · [dim][/dim]after planner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]flat-panes: add hood/family context queries for the Artifacts Agent pane[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and creating-agent context for Files, and make `agent:` jumps reveal [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]folded rows on the Agents tab, falling back to Artifacts ▸ Agent when [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the Agents-tab filter hides them.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stitch, Plan/provider, and Patch context queries[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bounded-panes[dim] · [dim][/dim]after planner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bounded-panes: acquire-then-reveal for panes whose inventory is bounded.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Stitch jumps rewrite to a repo-and-day window, Plan and provider panes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]use a `path:` context, and Patch jumps show the patch's stack, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Stitches' reveal row read from the unfiltered collection.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The reveal toast, lens chip, and user docs[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]toast[dim] · [dim][/dim]after planner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]toast: add a pure, escaped toast formatter showing the new query, what [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hid the target, the scope change, and the real restore/back keys, plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unified failure copy, a context label on the lens chip, and rewritten [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reveal-ladder docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One engine for every jump, plus the end-to-end matrix[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]entry-points[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flat-panes, bounded-panes, toast[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]entry-points: route relation-panel misses and cross-pane relation jumps [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the engine, fix `job:` jumps hidden by a collapsed scheduler [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fold and unconfigured provider kinds, and add a Links-panel-driven [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]end-to-end test matrix covering every artifact kind.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-16t","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-16t.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e52a59ec19feb45f284d550286ed14e2","started_at":"2026-09-23T12:25:58.257990+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1790169514,"sha":"f37f1dd480202d5eeead8aa04f8b0808504b8613","subject":"feat(query): wildcard parity, pin bump, pushdown guard, and docs (sase-16t.2, verification pending)"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"667d0c971940649903e653c6cf7f249d0b5a7cf76a2e9f28f350352d1aca0bb4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/chat.md","size_bytes":1885},"commits":{"digest":"b969dceed1898f76f1f4af43489a5f9027cd461c388af7af10c94a827f720b57","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/commits.json","size_bytes":277},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"0a0b6254074f4d141853c3955aeeaf738bdd6448ad2da304c41d77f6fa473627","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/meta.json","size_bytes":656},"prompt":{"digest":"c9241e8f4831459439fabaec4202e2888129542fbedc0017d94e34acb388723f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/prompt.md","size_bytes":145},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"9853374a4c1a459f81504777996e397b72a666673f6627a6415b675f22c2bb1f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":6004},"state":{"digest":"8bd7134f15fce4c906e637dc78708519c0b3b6d5112cdfc9de5f85afcf6ead35","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-09-23T13:20:47.606207+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-16t.2","local_name":"sase-16t.2","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-16t","agent_clan_generation":"20260923082509","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-